A directional look command is a good idea, and I think it should be bound
to the caret ^ .  It would then be downward compatible with the current
identify trap command.

Additionally, with this command you should be told what weapons the monster
is wielding.  An orc with a scimitar is a bit nastier than one carrying
only an orcish dagger, and there should be a way to discover this
information without letting yourself get clobbered first.

Something that would make nethack a bit easier (and 3.0 isn't getting many
complaints for being too easy) is to give a rough indication of how many
hit points a monster has left.  For instance,
bruised / bleeding / wounded / seriously wounded for
 75-99% /  50-74%  /  25-49% /  1-24%    of max hit points left.
You should be able to get a rough idea of how badly hurt a monster is by
looking at it.

